# WHAT: what never enters the Docker build context.
# WHY:  the context is the repo root, so without this every build ships ~74 MB
#       to the daemon — and, more importantly, ships `.env`. Nothing copies it
#       today (the Dockerfile takes only pyproject.toml, control/ and edge/), but
#       the first `COPY . .` anyone writes would bake real secrets into a layer.
#       This is the structural guard behind "never baked into an image layer"
#       in .claude/projects/04-infra-rulebook.md.
# HOW:  deny the risky and the useless; the Dockerfile names what it wants.

.env
*.key
*.pem
secrets/

.venv/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
tests/
.e2e/
*_cache/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
